<figure class="viz viz--roles" data-viz="government-roles-quadrant" id="roles">
  <figcaption class="viz__cap">
    <span class="viz__family">Government Roles Quadrant</span>
    <span class="viz__q">What role is government playing?</span>
  </figcaption>
  <ul class="roles-quad">
    <li>
      <strong>Rulemaker</strong>
      <span>Establishes the rules under which people and markets interact</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Provider</strong>
      <span>Provides genuine public goods and services where appropriate</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Investor / Owner</strong>
      <span>Holds productive assets only where public ownership is specifically justified</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Referee</strong>
      <span>Enforces rights, contracts, competition, and rules</span>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p class="viz__note">
    Do not casually blend roles. Owning a competitor while regulating rivals is a structural conflict
    for Stage 3 examination.
  </p>
</figure>
